# Backend environment for the NATIVE (Docker-free) local dev setup.
# Copy to backend/.env. This file is a template only — see scripts/manage-native.sh
# for the automated version (it sets these same variables for you).
#
# NOTE: python-dotenv is NOT installed or used by this project. The app reads env
# vars directly via os.getenv(). Before running uvicorn/neuro-api, export them:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
# or:
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)

# --- Database (single local Postgres 16 instance hosts both databases) ---
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/neurotoolkit
METADATA_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/neurotoolkit_metadata

# --- DICOM data ---
# Single root:
DATA_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/your/dicom/data
# Or multiple roots (JSON array string, takes precedence over DATA_ROOT):
# DATA_ROOTS=["/path/one","/path/two"]

# --- Optional: Body Part QC worker (disabled by default; CPU-only on macOS) ---
# Only needed if you run the worker via `scripts/manage-native.sh start --with-worker`.
# BODY_PART_WORKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8030

# --- Access control (optional) ---
# APP_ACCESS_TOKEN=change_me_to_a_secure_token

# --- Facility vault discovery (optional; required only to use the facility
# discovery scan/confirm endpoints) ---
# Root of the shared facility vault layout: <FACILITY_VAULT_ROOT>/mrc/sub-<id>,
# <FACILITY_VAULT_ROOT>/natmeg/<project>/raw/sub-<id>/<date> (an extra
# <acquisition> directory between `raw` and `sub-<id>` is also supported, if
# present, but is not required). Required to use POST /api/facility-discovery/scan.
# FACILITY_VAULT_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/vault
# Facility-maintained cross-facility subject/project mapping CSV (server-side path,
# fully reloaded on every discovery scan -- no upload endpoint in v1). Required
# to use POST /api/facility-discovery/scan.
# FACILITY_MAPPING_CSV_PATH=/absolute/path/to/facility-mapping.csv
# Per-project symlink staging root for the `mrc` facility. The directory itself
# is auto-created on disk if missing, but this env var has no default and MUST
# be set to confirm an `mrc` discovery (not required for `natmeg`). `mrc` has no
# on-disk project segmentation, so confirmed subjects are staged here.
# MRC_STAGING_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/mrc-staging
# Directory of generated per-cohort subject-code override CSVs. The directory
# itself is auto-created on disk if missing, but this env var has no default
# and MUST be set to confirm a discovery of EITHER facility. NILS writes one
# small 2-column CSV per cohort here (<cohort_id>.csv) mapping the real
# facility identifier (DICOM PatientID for `mrc`, MEG participant ID for
# `natmeg`) to the CIR subject code from FACILITY_MAPPING_CSV_PATH, and wires
# it into the existing extract/meg_scan CSV-override mechanism so extraction
# uses the CIR ID as the subject code instead of the raw facility identifier.
# This is NILS's own generated output, not a duplicate of the facility's input
# mapping sheet -- without it, extraction would use the raw facility ID.
# FACILITY_SUBJECT_CODE_CSV_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/facility-subject-code-csvs